{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1090037-looking-for-aphrodisia-like-art-in-c20","id":1090037,"title":"Looking for Aphrodisia-like Art in C20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-08T17:11:24-07:00","id":1090037,"title":"Looking for Aphrodisia-like Art in C20","content":"Of the three Merfolk arts, Skycraft came in pretty much As-Is and Kryos got remade into Winter. Aphrodisia is the only one I can't really see a replacement for in the core rules, though I was told it was there, just reinvisioned. I'm not really seeing it here..... Am I missing it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T17:12:55-07:00","id":1090038,"title":"","content":"Oh wait, there it is. Looks like some parts of it (the main gist of the power, really) was folded into Summer arts...... Guess some other aspects can come through Naming and Sovereign. Odd....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T17:47:32-07:00","id":1090057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagusRogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1090037-looking-for-aphrodisia-like-art-in-c20?p=1090038#post1090038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh wait, there it is. Looks like some parts of it (the main gist of the power, really) was folded into Summer arts...... Guess some other aspects can come through Naming and Sovereign. Odd....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In general, we worked to diversify the effects of Arts and to eliminate Arts whose powers replaced themselves (5th dot = more potent version of 4 = more potent version of 3, etc.). We also wanted to limit and define mind/emotion-control powers as they can be problematic. <br /> <br /> We broke down the Arts and listed themes and ideas in each one. The Arts that didn't get included we made an effort to fold their functionality into included Arts with overlapping themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13387-jonsan","name":"jonsan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T22:26:10-07:00","id":1090122,"title":"","content":"Eh don't mind it at all. Think most of the arts are cool, especially the new seasonal ones. And glad the stuff from blood dimmed tides made it in. Still a little salty about inanimae losing their cantrips but can't win them all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3071-magusrogue","name":"MagusRogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3071_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T02:04:18-07:00","id":1090184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagusRogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1090037-looking-for-aphrodisia-like-art-in-c20?p=1090122#post1090122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh don't mind it at all. Think most of the arts are cool, especially the new seasonal ones. And glad the stuff from blood dimmed tides made it in. Still a little salty about inanimae losing their cantrips but can't win them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those cantrips still exist in Inanimae: The Secret Way. I think it's not really that they've been retconned out, but rather that space requirements mean they've simplified the rules for the core book. Until we get a Book of the Gallain, you can use the old cantrips without it changing anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}